 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 666811,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which code prints each number in <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">my_list</code> starting from <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">7</code>, then <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">4</code>, and so on ending with <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">-5</code>?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1329447,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">for row in my_list:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;for elem in row:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;print(elem)\n</pre>",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "The outer <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">for</code> loop iterates row by row. The inner <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">for</code> loop iterates through each element in a row. So all the numbers are printed, starting from 7 and ending in -5."
    },
    {
     "id": 1329448,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">for elem in my_list:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;print(elem)\n</pre>\n",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "The for loop prints each element in my_list, so it prints the list <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">[7, 4, 5, 12]</code>, followed by <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">[24, 3, 9, 16]</code> and finally <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">[12, 8, 91, -5]</code> not the individual numbers."
    }
   ],
